Package: devjam-desktop-kernel-hardening
Version: 1.0-4
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: Kernel hardening sysctl settings for desktops
 sysctl settings that harden the kernel without affecting latency: they
 hide kernel pointers, harden the BPF JIT, restrict perf events,
 maximise ASLR entropy, limit oops and warning loops, and protect FIFOs
 and core dumps of setuid programs.
